Adaptive safe-viewport macdriver delta (wine-adaptive-macdriver)

Opt-in macdrv changes for RA3_SAFE_VIEWPORT (raw Wine units, exclusive
edges, e.g. 3024x1964:0,64,3024,1964), against the accepted five-patch
fixed-viewport tree (wine 11.0, branch tip 3562fea). Shared header
include/wine/ra3_viewport.h is delivered separately by the candidate
tree; this patch contains exactly the three winemac.drv file deltas:

- window.c: macdrv_client_surface_update gate generalized: valid
  RA3_SAFE_VIEWPORT -> adaptive route; present but invalid -> neither
  adaptive nor legacy (stock); absent -> legacy exact RA3_FIXED_VIEWPORT
  "3024x1900" route, body unchanged.
- cocoa_window.m: setMask same gate, conversion still cgrect_mac_from_win
  (Wine binary raw->Cocoa scaling, not screen backing scale).
  WineMetalView opt-in backing scale: setRetinaMode re-sets contentsScale
  to window.backingScaleFactor after super; makeBackingLayer falls back
  to the primary screen's actual backing scale (window screen first, then
  CGMainDisplayID identity match via NSScreenNumber); viewDidMoveToWindow
  and viewDidChangeBackingProperties (NSView, macOS 10.7.4+) refresh it.
  With no valid RA3_SAFE_VIEWPORT every new branch is inert.
- display.c: ra3_adaptive_retina_2x() helper - active only when a valid
  RA3_SAFE_VIEWPORT names the native panel size AND the live main display
  mode is its 2x variant (rotation-normalized per 90/270 like
  display_mode_to_devmode_fields; live mode never cached). While active,
  retina 2x doubling is forced regardless of the startup descriptor in
  copy_display_modes/create_mode_dict (main display only), check_retina_status,
  find_best_display_mode, display_get_modes and display_get_current_mode.
  Absent/invalid variable: no condition changes anywhere.

Main-display-only guards in copy_display_modes/display_get_modes keep
non-primary displays on the stock descriptor logic. No ABI/struct
changes; mask window transform keeps the Wine 2x scale; mtld3d is
untouched. Hotplug and mid-session display-mode changes are explicitly
unverified.

